{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>ושמתיה [I will set it]. קפוד [bittern/porcupine].</b> It is known — some say it is from the root of קפדתי כאורג חיי (Isaiah 38:12), because of His anger." "<b>וטאטאתיה [I will sweep it].</b> All the commentators say that this word has no cognate, and the meaning is the tool with which they remove dirt."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "Resolved the phrase יש אומרים as introducing a reported opinion; the pun depends on קפד/קפידה (anger)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:49.611085130Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}